18667453-7e89-4609-8b56-16aa401e9e7b	dd397028-e71b-4c35-9b40-95f7115f39b5	92	To resolve the N+1 query problem, I utilize Eager Loading to fetch all required related data in a single initial query rather than executing individual database hits for each item in a collection. By using techniques like joinedload in SQLAlchemy (or similar include methods in other ORMs), I force the database to perform a JOIN or a separate efficient IN query, which significantly reduces latency. For instance, instead of looping through users and querying their posts one-by-one, I refactor the code to select(User).options(joinedload(User.posts)), ensuring all posts are loaded into memory immediately, which eliminates redundant database roundtrips and optimizes overall performance.	The answer is highly technical, precise, and demonstrates both theoretical knowledge (Eager Loading) and practical implementation details (specific ORM syntax).	surgical-feedback-v1.4	f	[{"id": "TD2", "name": "Practical Application", "score": 95, "weight": 0.4166666666666667}, {"id": "TD4", "name": "Code Quality & Best Practices", "score": 90, "weight": 0.33333333333333337}, {"id": "TD5", "name": "Debug & Problem-solving", "score": 90, "weight": 0.25}]	2026-07-03 11:29:10.088+07
