cf4092e8-0bf4-4686-9bcb-2a2de173c5eb	fb1f82d2-0ded-4f07-9b18-579d1da1279f	62	To isolate the root cause, I utilized distributed tracing (Jaeger) and analyzed database transaction logs, which revealed that multiple concurrent API calls were attempting to acquire pessimistic locks on the same resource without proper transaction isolation levels. The core issue was a race condition leading to deadlocks when two services tried to book adjacent slots simultaneously. To prevent recurrence, we refactored the booking logic to use optimistic locking with version numbers and implemented an asynchronous message queue (Kafka) for all slot reservation requests, ensuring sequential processing.	The candidate successfully set up the 'Situation' but must dedicate equal time and technical depth to describing the debugging process (tools/logs) and the architectural fix.	surgical-feedback-v1.4	f	[{"id": "TD2", "name": "Practical Application", "score": 65, "weight": 0.4166666666666667}, {"id": "TD3", "name": "Systems Thinking", "score": 60, "weight": 0.33333333333333337}, {"id": "TD5", "name": "Debug & Problem-solving", "score": 60, "weight": 0.25}]	2026-07-03 11:32:20.787+07
